  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">infoDev  MTDF on innovation and entrepreneurship - Infodev</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">infoDev  multigivarfond inom innovation och entrepren&#xf6;rskap</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobile subscriptions recently reached 6 billion, and almost 75% of those are found in developing countries. But the potential of mobile phones in developing countries are still largely untapped. Mobile applications today are mainly related to sports, entertainment and music. They have great potential to foster inclusive growth, by giving access to services, products and markets to parts of the world unreachable through other existing infrastructure. Mobile phones can assist people living in poverty to improve their living conditions and it can provide access or removal of discriminatory barriers for vulnerable groups.The intervention targets the problem by trying to facilitate demand-driven, sustained and scalable mobile entrepreneurship and to jumpstart a thriving local mobile content industry which fosters social entrepreneurship. This will be done through the support and nurturing of innovative businesses in emerging markets. Key activities include the creation of mobile hubs (mHubs) which provide entrepreneurs with technical assistance, networking opportunities, capacity development, infrastructure (broadband and testing facilities) and office space.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till sociala entrepren&#xf6;rer inom mobilteknologi genom s.k. mobile  hubs och mobile laboratories (mHubs/mLabs). Syftet &#xe4;r att            mHubs/mLabs ska hj&#xe4;lpa entrepren&#xf6;rer att konkretisera och realisera   sina id&#xe9;er (from mind to market). S&#xe4;rskilt fokus p&#xe5; kvinnliga         entrepren&#xf6;rer och entrepren&#xf6;rer fr&#xe5;n botten av pyramiden (BoP).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to social entrepreneurs within mobile technology through      mobile hubs and mobile laboratories (mHubs/mLabs). The purpose is     that mHubs/mLabs should faciltiate the transfer of ideas from mind to market. Specific focus is on women entrepreneurs and entrepreneurs at the bottom of the pyramid (BoP).</narrative>
  </description>
